-\paragraph{Limitations.} Runs use one ReAct scaffold on \numModels{} open-weight models (4B--397B) at $T{=}0.1$; frontier APIs and broader $T$ sweeps are deferred (App.~\ref{app:temperature_sensitivity}). Scenarios are engine-synthetic, so absolute rates are engine-conditional. Three facts mitigate this. Thm.~\ref{thm:coarsening} is distribution-independent. A Tier~S expansion (+\tierSExtraCPGs{}~CPGs, +\tierSExtraEpisodes{}~episodes) preserves every reported metric within $\pm$\tierSMaxMetricShift{}\,pp. A Phase~B auto-expansion (\numTotalScenarios{} scenarios, \phaseBEpisodes{} episodes, $4.5{\times}$ the manual 706-scenario base) tightens cell-level pair-reversal from $46.3$\% to $\cellPairReversal{}$\% and preserves the typed-CwT $\eta^{2}_{\mathrm{eval}}{>}\eta^{2}_{\mathrm{run}}$ ordering (\S\ref{sec:robustness_summary}). The load-bearing real-data probe is the pre-registered MIMIC-IV re-scoring (App.~\ref{app:dandb_ethics}), deferred. Clinician adjudication of catalogue-flagged violations is in progress and is not used as evidence for the present submission; the claims here are observation-level mis-certification relative to a source-traceable guideline catalogue, not clinical-safety judgement. Four standing threats (scaffold, engine realism, held-out, clinician-pending) admit falsifiable probes (Table~\ref{tab:defense}). Three v6 disclosures (nemotron empty 0.99\%, Step-11 LLM-judge substitute, gemma31b auto\_v2 only) are documented in App.~\ref{app:v6_disclosures}.
+\paragraph{Limitations.} Runs use one ReAct scaffold on \numModels{} open-weight models (4B--397B) at $T{=}0.1$; frontier APIs and broader $T$ sweeps are deferred (App.~\ref{app:temperature_sensitivity}). Scenarios are engine-synthetic, so absolute rates are engine-conditional. Three facts mitigate this. Thm.~\ref{thm:coarsening} is distribution-independent. A Tier~S expansion (+\tierSExtraCPGs{}~CPGs, +\tierSExtraEpisodes{}~episodes) preserves every reported metric within $\pm$\tierSMaxMetricShift{}\,pp. A Phase~B auto-expansion (\numTotalScenarios{} scenarios, \phaseBEpisodes{} episodes, $4.5{\times}$ the manual 706-scenario base) tightens cell-level pair-reversal from $46.3$\% to $\cellPairReversal{}$\% and preserves the typed-CwT $\eta^{2}_{\mathrm{eval}}{>}\eta^{2}_{\mathrm{run}}$ ordering (\S\ref{sec:robustness_summary}). The load-bearing real-data probe is the pre-registered MIMIC-IV re-scoring (App.~\ref{app:dandb_ethics}), deferred. Systematic clinician adjudication of catalogue-flagged violations is in progress and is not used as scoring evidence for the present submission; one validator-surfaced finding has been integrated as a catalogue-curation refinement (v1.1 patch, App.~\ref{app:conflict_patch}), but pairwise alignment scoring against clinician verdicts is deferred. The claims here are observation-level mis-certification relative to a source-traceable guideline catalogue, not clinical-safety judgement. Four standing threats (scaffold, engine realism, held-out, clinician-pending) admit falsifiable probes (Table~\ref{tab:defense}). Three v6 disclosures (nemotron empty 0.99\%, Step-11 LLM-judge substitute, gemma31b auto\_v2 only) are documented in App.~\ref{app:v6_disclosures}.
 
 \paragraph{Iterative refinement under expert review (v1.1 patch).}
 Clinician validation surfaced one massive-PE scenario where the runtime engine---by construction evaluating only static \texttt{mandatory\_actions}/\texttt{forbidden\_actions} lists, not the per-node \texttt{conditional\_rules} block---assigned full credit despite an action being simultaneously required and contraindicated under co-satisfiable conditions. We address this by coupling the Constraint Derivation Engine into the scoring path (App.~\ref{app:conflict_patch}): episode trajectories are unchanged, but violation extraction now consumes both engine-derived and CDE-derived constraints and emits a new \emph{conflict} violation type when an action is mandated and forbidden simultaneously. A static audit across all \cdeAuditCpgsTotal{}~CPGs identifies \conflictPatternsN{} same-action conflict patterns spanning \conflictGraphsN{} graphs (Tier~A/B/C: \tierAN{}/\tierBN{}/\tierCN{}; App.~\ref{app:conflict_patch}). The patch is strictly additive: with the feature flag off, scoring is byte-identical to v1.0 (regression-guarded by \texttt{tests/test\_assessor/test\_cde\_rescoring\_regression.py}); the \strictFAThree{}\% headline is preserved while CONFLICT events are now reported separately as a sixth sub-construct. This demonstrates the operational value of the audit-not-validation framing: the framework surfaces its own catalogue gaps under expert review.
